            <ArticleTitle>Klippel-Feil syndrome associated with posterior fossa dermoid cyst. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>501-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with association of Klippel-Feil syndrome and posterior fossa dermoid cyst is presented. The patient, a 36-year-old man, presented with an acute obstructive hydrocephalus due to the cyst and exhibited the typical triad of the Klippel-Feil abnormality with short neck, low hairline implantation and limited neck motion along with a complex cervical vertebrae fusion. The anatomical and clinical features as well as the pathophysiology of this rare association are discussed after a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
